            <ArticleTitle>Clinicopathological Profile of Childhood Primary Abdominal Tumours in Kashmir.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>361-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12262-013-0843-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary abdominal tumours attract considerable notice because of their serious prognosis, high cost of treatment and the emotional and psychological trauma. Abdominal tumours can present with pain, vomiting, constipation or less commonly intestinal obstruction. The presentation of cancer in children mimic those of childhood conditions like infections particularly viral infections, urinary tract infections, gastro-oesophageal reflux, malnutrition, constipation, lymphadnenitis, glomerulonephritis and congenital urinary tract anomalies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
